     "reply": "```json\n{\n  \"file\": \"data/run_log.xlsx\",\n  \"sheets\": \"주간요약\",\n  \"chart\": \"bar\",\n  \"x\": \"주차\",\n  \"y\": \"총생산량(kg)\",\n  \"code\": \"bars = ax.patches\\nfor i, bar in enumerate(bars):\\n    week_num = int(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2)\\n    if week_num >= 14:\\n        bar.set_facecolor('orange')\\n    else:\\n        bar.set_facecolor('steelblue')\\n\\n# Data for averaging: '총생산량(kg)' column from the sheet used in chart\\nimport pandas as pd\\n# Re-load data to calculate averages precisely based on original sheet values\\n# Note: In plotkit sandbox, we can often access the underlying dataframe or use the drawn data.\\n# Assuming 'data' variable holds the plotted series or we can reconstruct it. \\n# Safer approach using matplotlib and numpy with known x-axis (1-26) and y-values from bars.\\ny_vals = [b.get_height() for b in bars]\\nx_vals = [int(b.get_x() + b.get_width()/2) for b in bars]\\n\\nmask_pre = [x < 14 for x in x_vals]\\nmask_post = [x >= 14 for x in x_vals]\\n\\navg_pre = sum(y for x, y in zip(x_vals, y_vals) if x < 14) / len([x for x in x_vals if x < 14])\\navg_post = sum(y for x, y in zip(x_vals, y_vals) if x >= 14) / len([x for x in x_vals if x >= 14])\\n\\nax.axhline(avg_pre, color='gray', linestyle='--', linewidth=1.5, label=f'1~13주 평균 ({avg_pre:.1f})')\\nax.axhline(avg_post, color='black', linestyle='-', linewidth=1.5, label=f'14~26주 평균 ({avg_post:.1f})')\\nax.legend(loc='upper right')\",\n  \"asks\": [\n    {\n      \"ask\": \"14주차부터 색 구분\",\n      \"how\": \"code\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ask\": \"기간별 평균 가로선\",\n      \"how\": \"code\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
